      "writtenOn": "2024-12-10T19:53:12Z",
      "side": 1,
      "message": "Great, that\u0027s what I suspected but I wanted to be sure.\n\nMaybe to avoid passing in the Adapter we could pass a SupportedLimits object instead? But I don\u0027t think there is one that lives anywhere that we could pass without having to create it (by calling APIGetLimits).\n\nI suppose maybe we could have a base class of Adapter that _only_ provides APIGetLimits and pass that in.\n\nAbout `const`, would it work (and would it help) to use `CacheKey::UnsafeUnkeyedValue\u003cconst dawn::native::AdapterBase*\u003e` instead?",
      "parentUuid": "b83edf9b_33297d6f",
